#
# Conformance case: foundation/weak-supplementation
# AC: holon kernel — profile-scoped weak supplementation (issue #704, C1).
#
# Weak supplementation (a whole with a proper part has another proper part
# disjoint from the first) is a logic:MereologyConstraint, NOT an OntoUML
# logic:Discipline: it holds only within a declared logic:MereologyProfile, never
# across all parthood. The prerequisites logic:overlaps and logic:disjoint are
# settled first, so the axiom never fires where overlap is undefined.
#   * ex:W1 — declared under ex:MP with a LONE proper part ex:P1 (no disjoint
#     co-part) → logic:violation logic:WeakSupplementation.
#   * ex:W2 — declared under ex:MP with TWO disjoint proper parts ex:Pa, ex:Pb
#     (they share no part) → each has a disjoint co-part → trips nothing.
#   * ex:W3 — a lone proper part ex:P3 but NOT declared under any profile →
#     parthood is profiled, so no supplementation obligation applies (inert).
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so the parthood +
# profile edges are duplicated there in the named world ex:schema.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/weak-supplementation/> .

# Schema (also world facts in input.nq).
ex:MP a logic:MereologyProfile .
ex:W1 logic:underMereologyProfile ex:MP .
ex:P1 logic:properPartOf ex:W1 .
ex:W2 logic:underMereologyProfile ex:MP .
ex:Pa logic:properPartOf ex:W2 .
ex:Pb logic:properPartOf ex:W2 .
ex:P3 logic:properPartOf ex:W3 .
